@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/streams/[stream_uuid]/actions/read/invoke
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceStreamController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Scope workers\nlease + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/streams/{stream_uuid}/actions/read/invoke
API -> DB: Readings are in order . + immutable outbox event\nFor each exact-scope task
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: the event that was recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: read_counters / folder_projection\neach exact-scope task It has its own outbox_event_uuid
Worker -> Worker: One fenced owner exact scope; - A lot of different ones . scopes parallel to each other
Worker -> Projection: The topic/stream/folder binding counters
Worker -> Events: stream.read + container events\natomically in one. DB transaction with a projection
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
note over Worker,Projection
  Topic worker shared counters He doesn 't write ..
  Atomic delta It requires exactly-once guard; Otherwise recompute/write.
  Retry/backoff, DLQ/reaper - They 're compulsory ..
end note
@enduml
